{"scenario":"pool-after-deploy","description":"inventory pool exhaustion right after an unrelated, healthy inventory release","mode":"graph","recorded_at":"2026-10-18 04:00","duration":90.29,"agent":{"duration_s":49.6,"tool_calls":11,"cost_usd":0.15456380000000003,"input_tokens":105431,"output_tokens":3350,"report":"## INC-043 resolved: frontend is back to 0% errors\n\n**Root cause:** inventory ran out of database connections (`psycopg_pool.PoolTimeout`: pool size 10, all 10 in use, 37 requests waiting). This matches a known connection leak documented in runbook RB-INV-01 and past incident INC-019, tracked for a code fix as PLAT-212. No single change caused it, so the incident is resolved without a root-cause change id.\n\n**Evidence path:** `frontend` \u2192 `catalog` / `checkout` \u2192 `inventory` (connection pool exhausted)\n- inventory is the deepest failing service, and its own dependencies are healthy. 96 of its 199 requests failed inside inventory itself.\n- catalog, checkout and frontend were failing only because inventory was. None of their errors started in those services.\n- 99 of the 101 recent inventory log lines are the same `PoolTimeout` error.\n\n**Changes I did not treat as the cause:**\n- **inventory v5.1.2** (chg-3fb18229, deployed by sam at 22:15, \"pgbouncer config bump\"): the runbook says the leak is in every current release, and that rolling back would only revert a healthy release. The errors also started about 14 minutes after the deploy, which looks more like a leak building up than a broken config.\n- **checkout v4.2.1** (chg-b015bfe4): checkout's errors all came from inventory.\n\n**Action taken (1 of 3 allowed):** restarted `inventory` as the runbook says, first as a dry run and then for real.\n\n**Verification:** frontend error rate went 15% \u2192 0% \u2192 0%, and it was marked healthy about 7 seconds after the restart. p95 latency stayed around 113ms.\n\n**Paged:** sam, platform team on-call (#team-platform). No webhook is configured, so the page was only recorded in the graph and sam hasn't actually been notified. The page asks them to:\n- prioritise PLAT-212, since this is the second time this has happened and it will keep happening until the leak is fixed;\n- confirm v5.1.2 didn't make the pool run out faster.","start_t":27.46,"end_t":77.78},"events":[{"t":0.06,"kind":"start","text":"healthy baseline"},{"t":3.1,"kind":"inject","text":"inventory pool exhaustion right after an unrelated, healthy inventory release"},{"t":27.46,"kind":"alert","text":"ALERT frontend error rate 50%, p95 113ms"},{"t":27.46,"kind":"agent","text":"headless agent started (graph mode)"},{"t":77.78,"kind":"done","text":"agent finished"}],"steps":[{"t":30.09,"n":1,"tool":"rank_suspects","note":"top suspect inventory (score 0.901) via path frontend -> catalog -> inventory","targets":["Service:checkout","Service:frontend","Service:inventory","Service:payment","Change:chg-b015bfe4","Change:chg-3fb18229"]},{"t":31.72,"n":2,"tool":"get_logs","note":"read 101 log entries of inventory","targets":["Service:inventory"]},{"t":32.08,"n":3,"tool":"find_similar_incidents","note":"3 similar past incidents, best INC-019","targets":["Incident:INC-019","Incident:INC-027","Incident:INC-031"]},{"t":38.83,"n":4,"tool":"get_owner","note":"inventory is owned by platform (on call: sam)","targets":["Service:inventory","Team:platform","Person:sam","Runbook:RB-INV-01"]},{"t":38.83,"n":5,"tool":"recent_changes","note":"1 changes in last 60 min around inventory","targets":["Service:inventory","Change:chg-3fb18229"]},{"t":44.77,"n":6,"tool":"open_incident","note":"INC-043: Frontend 50% errors: inventory DB pool exhaustion","targets":["Incident:INC-043"]},{"t":46.85,"n":7,"tool":"restart_service","note":"DRY RUN restart inventory","targets":["Service:inventory"]},{"t":49.35,"n":8,"tool":"restart_service","note":"RESTARTED inventory","targets":["Service:inventory","Action:act-0736217e"]},{"t":60.7,"n":9,"tool":"verify_recovery","note":"frontend RECO